          "filename": "Kinshasa & Brazzaville - ISS007-E-6305 lrg.jpg",
          "caption": "Satellite picture of the Pool Malebo section of the Congo River. Also of Brazzaville (north bank), and Kinshasa (southwest bank). \n\"Caption: Kinshasa and Brazzaville: This image, taken from the International Space Station on June 6, 2003, shows two capital cities on opposite banks of the Congo River. The smaller city is Brazzaville on the north side of the river, and Kinshasa on the south side. The cities lie at the downstream end of an almost circular widening in the river known as Stanley Pool. The international boundary follows the south shore of the pool (roughly 30 km in diameter).\"\n\nMission: ISS007, Roll: E, Frame: 6305",
